{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "summary": "Warcraft III MDX/MDL decoding is a port, not a rewrite. The format layer is the MIT war3-model 4.0.1 parser/generator, vendored under a compatibility profile; the adapter above it came from the MK2 war3-mdx implementation and is now ordinary MK3 code that compiles under this package strict profile.",
  "mk2Removed": {
    "note": "This package carries no MK2 tree any more. The adapter moved into src/war3-mdx, and the MK2 game-discovery copy was replaced by an MK3 common.game/installation-discovery provider in src/game/installation.ts rather than being kept as an unresolvable copy.",
    "paths": [
      "src/lib/mk2/war3-mdx/** -> src/war3-mdx/{detect,render-model}.ts",
      "src/lib/mk2/games/warcraft-3/** -> src/game/installation.ts (rewritten for MK3)",
      "test/mk2/** -> deleted; the oracle copies could not resolve their MK2-only imports"
    ]
  },
  "upstream": {
    "war3-model": {
      "version": "4.0.1",
      "license": "MIT",
      "licenseFile": "licenses/war3-model-MIT.txt",
      "readFrom": "references/war3-model",
      "omitted": [
        "blp/** — Modkit reads BLP through the blizzard/blp codec",
        "renderer/** — Modkit renders through @modkit/scene; only the two layer-texture maps were taken, into src/lib/war3-model/layer-textures.ts"
      ]
    },
    "modkit-mk2": {
      "readFrom": "references/modkitmk2/extensions/blizzard/warcraft-3/codecs/war3-mdx",
      "manifestStatus": "supported",
      "note": "MK2 consumed war3-model as an npm dependency; MK3 vendors the sources instead so the extension keeps no external runtime dependency."
    },
    "mdx-m3-viewer": {
      "commit": "2ff0bc00c6363f425016e23d88c0fb2929d3b3cc",
      "license": "MIT",
      "licenseFile": "licenses/mdx-m3-viewer-MIT.txt",
      "readFrom": "references/mdx-m3-viewer/src",
      "decision": "Owner 2026-09-28 (Q1 of docs/MK3/PLAN_WARCRAFT3_FORMATS_2026-09-28.md): vendor the map-document parsers with provenance.",
      "omitted": [
        "parsers/w3x/map.ts — the map archive is read through the blizzard/mpq container",
        "parsers/w3x/wts — trigger strings have their own parser in src/wts",
        "parsers/w3x/{wtg,wct} — GUI triggers need TriggerData.txt and the JASS token stream; a later stage",
        "parsers/w3x/w3f — campaign info (.w3n), not read yet",
        "common/* other than binarystream, bytesof, searches, typecast, utf8"
      ]
    }
  },
  "edits": [
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/{model.ts,mdx/parse.ts,mdx/generate.ts,mdl/parse.ts}",
      "change": "Retain an authored static EmissiveGainFallback separately before KMTE overwrites the animated property; MDX regenerates that header instead of hardcoded 1. Existing MDL parser acceptance retains static/track records in either order, but no new MDL syntax is emitted.",
      "why": "A bounded native 1100 fixture with static header 0 and unchanged KMTE keys wrote header 1 through model.write and UVM reconstruction. Public game writer wrappers validate the finite exact float32 fallback profile (negative zero excluded), reject conflicting/invalid carriers and refuse non-default static headers beside KMTE in MDL until native grammar is qualified. Missing legacy carriers retain compatibility default 1, not a recovered source value. No reference implementation copied; native Editor, playback/default semantics and adjacent Fresnel header preservation remain unqualified."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/{model.ts,mdx/parse.ts,mdx/generate.ts,mdl/parse.ts,mdl/generate.ts}",
      "change": "KRCO is a ribbon FLOAT3 animation track, represented by the same AnimVector as other native tracks; MDX size/read/write and MDL RGB/BGR channel conversion include its keys and tangents. ColorFallback preserves the independent static header value beside an animated track.",
      "why": "The previous reader refused KRCO and its writer could not re-emit animated ribbon colors. Format facts checked against the existing mdx-m3-viewer ribbon parser/viewer; no reference implementation copied."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/**",
      "change": "extensionless relative specifiers rewritten to explicit '.js' for NodeNext, and '../renderer/util' redirected to the copied layer-textures module"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/war3-mdx/render-model.ts",
      "change": "imports rewritten for MK3: 'war3-model' -> '../lib/war3-model/index.js', '@modkitx/models-processing' -> '@modkit/codec-kit/legacy/models'; a header records the provenance"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/war3-mdx/render-model.ts",
      "change": "buildBounds now accepts undefined extents and returns null. An MDL that declares no extents previously threw a null dereference out of the codec."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/mdl/generate.ts",
      "change": "generateBoneChunk and the animation-vector writer guarded only against null, so an absent GeosetId, GeosetAnimId or GlobalSeqId was written as the literal text `undefined` and the emitted MDL no longer parsed. Both now treat absent as null."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/mdx/generate.ts",
      "change": "The same null-only guard as the MDL writer, in binary: an absent GlobalSeqId, TVertexAnimId, GeosetId, GeosetAnimId, ObjectId, Parent or emitter TextureID was written as 0 instead of -1. Every track of a converted model then ran on a global sequence 0 the model does not declare, and each clip read back carried the keys of the whole timeline. All eight sites now write -1 for absent (`?? NONE`)."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/mdx/parse.ts",
      "change": "The fixed-length string reader trimmed trailing NULs only, so a padded field followed by any non-NUL byte returned the padding and the stray bytes. It now ends the string at the first NUL, as a C string does."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/war3-model/mdx/parse.ts, src/lib/war3-model/mdx/generate.ts, src/lib/war3-model/model.ts",
      "change": "An event object's KEVT global sequence id was read and dropped as 'unused' and written as -1. It is kept as EventObject.GlobalSeqId and written back (2026-10-09), as mdx-m3-viewer reads it: a global-sequence event fires every cycle."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/war3-mdx/render-model.ts",
      "change": "buildWar3AttachmentMetadata and buildWar3CollisionMetadata also record `ownNodeIndex`, the node each attachment or collision shape IS rather than the bone it hangs on.",
      "why": "A writer rebuilding an ATCH or CLID record from the common scene needs to know which node carries it; without this the MK3 UVM export had nowhere to mark them and both were dropped on any document without our own residual."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/mdx-m3-viewer/**",
      "change": "extensionless relative specifiers rewritten to explicit '.js' (or '/index.js') for NodeNext; CRLF line endings of upstream files stored as LF"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/mdx-m3-viewer/{common/binarystream.ts,parsers/w3x/w3i/randomunittable.ts,parsers/w3x/wpm/file.ts}",
      "change": "typed-array fields annotated (ArrayBuffer | Uint8Array, Int32Array, Uint8Array) so the TypeScript 5.7 generic typed-array lib accepts them; no behaviour changed"
    }
  ],
